    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "LIFECYCLE EVENTS\n\nThree built-in events drive a class through its life:\n  Begin Play  runs once when the object enters the game.\n  On Tick     runs every frame and receives the time since the last frame (Get Delta Time).\n  On End Play runs once when the object leaves the game or the session ends.\nVariables keep their values between these events, which is how a Blueprint remembers things.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "BEGIN PLAY\nOnce, at the start. Mark the phase and announce it.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -50.0
        ],
        "size": [
          840.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "ph1",
          "hi"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "ON TICK\nEvery frame: count it and remember how long it took. Get Delta Time is a pure node valid inside Tick. (Decimal addition is not a built-in node; use it with Lerp, Mean etc. when you need to accumulate time.)",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          440.0
        ],
        "size": [
          840.0,
          120.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
